font-style: inherit;">0</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">,</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1023</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">,</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">30</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">,</span> <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">100</span><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">);</span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>Reads the variable resistor and calculates target minimum distance using <code>map()</code>. This lets me adjust the parking distance with just a screwdriver!</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Distance Measurement</strong></p>
<div class="sourceCode" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode cpp code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode cpp"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="dt" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">long</span> distance <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> readDist<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">();</span></span></code></pre></div>
<p>Calls <code>readDist()</code> to get current distance to the wall.</p></li>
<li><p><strong>LED Display Logic</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Max distance capped at <code>distMax = 250</code> → calls <code>showmax()</code></li>
<li>Distance ≤ <code>minDist</code> → calls <code>showmin()</code></li>
<li>Everything else → activates appropriate number of LEDs</li>
</ul></li>
<li><p><strong>Sleep Management</strong> Checks if it’s time to sleep by comparing current <code>millis()</code> with <code>SLEEPDELAY</code>.</p></li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="key-functions" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="key-functions">Key Functions</h3>
<p><strong>readDist()</strong> - Returns average of 10 readings (configurable via <code>numReadings</code>). Max distance hard-coded to 250cm.</p>
<p><strong>showmin()</strong> - Accepts float ‘d’ (ratio of distance to <code>distMin</code>). As the car gets closer beyond safe distance, ‘d’ gets smaller and green LEDs flash faster. Drama! 🎭</p>
<p><strong>showmax()</strong> - Simply indicates the car is still out of range.</p>
</section>
</section>
<section id="step-4-implementation" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-4-implementation">Step 4: Implementation</h2>
<p>The final system looks clean and professional. All boards are designed to be as visually appealing as possible, and I think it turned out really well!</p>
</section>
